# What never reaches the build context.
#
# Two jobs. Most of this is about size and cache hits — a local `node_modules`
# copied in would be both the largest thing in the context and the reason every
# build invalidates its own layers. The `.env.*` lines are about something else
# entirely, and are the important ones.

# Installed in the image by `npm ci`, from the lockfile. A host copy would be
# the wrong platform's binaries as often as not.
node_modules
npm-debug.log*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- secrets --
# `.env.production` and `.env.development` are tracked in this repository and
# carry a database password, both JWT secrets and the super admin's password.
# The image is pushed to a public registry, where `docker history` and a single
# `docker run --entrypoint cat` would read any of them straight back out.
#
# The API does not need them: `src/config/env.js` loads an env file only when
# one exists and lets the real process environment win regardless, so the
# container is configured with `--env-file`, a compose `environment:` block or
# the orchestrator's own secrets.
.env
.env.*

# --------------------------------------------------------------- runtime --
# Written by the running service, not built into it. Mount volumes instead.
uploads
logs
*.log
*.sqlite

# ------------------------------------------------------------ not the app --
.git
.gitignore
.github
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
README.md
coverage
dist
.vscode
.idea
.DS_Store
